From f839e0fed76beceb9a82fdaf7d30024b08b1065f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaiRat <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:42:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Route all Unicode-mode patterns to Broiler; unify match data;
 fall back on overflow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four track-2 changes on the Broiler.JS side of the RegExp integration.

Routing (actions 5 and 6): the router — now TryRouteToBroiler — routes every Unicode-mode
(u/v) pattern Broiler can build, not just the gap shapes. A JSRegExp-level differential
against V8 found the bugs this fixes for non-gap Unicode patterns: a standalone \p{…} under
`i` threw a SyntaxError, and in-class case folding was missed (/[α-ω]/iu did not match `µ`,
which folds to μ). Non-Unicode patterns stay on the mature, far faster .NET engine — the
common ASCII/hot-loop case — until the matcher is optimized. `UsesUnsupported` is gone; the
v-mode class-set and in-class property shapes it once refused are now evaluated by Broiler.

Match data (action 4): exec already read either engine through RunMatch; now Split and
Replace do too, via a shared EnumerateMatches iterator (code-point-aware empty-match
advance, lastIndex left untouched). The legacy String.prototype.split/replace fallback and
assert.match answer through the routed engine, and IJSRegExp.Value is retired for an
engine-agnostic IsMatch.

Null-tolerant translation (tail of action 4): CreateRegex runs with a null value when a
transform or new Regex cannot represent a routed pattern, so a v-mode set operation over a
built-in class escape ([\s&&\S], [\d&&\s], [\s--\d]) — valid ECMAScript the .NET UnicodeSets
translator rejects — now constructs and matches through Broiler.

Overflow fallback: Broiler's continuation-passing matcher recurses per quantifier
iteration, so a repeat over a long subject would overflow the stack. RunMatch catches the
RegexOverflowException the Broiler patch throws and falls back to the iterative .NET engine
for that subject (or reports no match when the pattern has no .NET translation).

RegExpUnicodeRoutingTests, RegExpEngineConsistencyTests and RegExpTranslatorFallbackTests
cover these. A 12,792-case JSRegExp-level differential against V8 — including long subjects
that exercise the fallback — leaves only the two documented deliberate vi divergences.
BuiltIns.Tests 2204 (up from 2173); Integration 5024 of 5025 (the one failure,
M8_DocumentationFiles_Exist, is pre-existing and unrelated).

Requires the matching Broiler.Regex revision (its RegexOverflowException,
CharSet.UsesPropertyEscape and MatchesEmptyString).
